WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:07.910 --> 00:00:10.110
- Are you excited by the thing

00:00:10.110 --> 00:00:13.160
that Elon Musk is doing
with SpaceX in general,

00:00:13.160 --> 00:00:14.920
with the idea of space exploration,

00:00:14.920 --> 00:00:18.660
even though your species
is young and impatient?

00:00:18.660 --> 00:00:21.300
- Yeah, I do think that space travel

00:00:21.300 --> 00:00:24.110
is crucially important long-term,

00:00:24.110 --> 00:00:26.920
even to other star systems, and I think

00:00:26.920 --> 00:00:31.520
that many people
overestimate the difficulty,

00:00:31.520 --> 00:00:33.910
because they say, look,
if you travel 1% the speed

00:00:33.910 --> 00:00:35.330
of light to another star system,

00:00:35.330 --> 00:00:37.370
we'll be dead before we get there, right?

00:00:37.370 --> 00:00:39.500
And I think that it's much easier,

00:00:39.500 --> 00:00:41.050
and therefore, when they
write their science fiction

00:00:41.050 --> 00:00:42.390
stories, they imagine we can go faster

00:00:42.390 --> 00:00:43.390
than the speed of light, 'cause otherwise

00:00:43.390 --> 00:00:45.010
they're too impatient, right?

00:00:45.010 --> 00:00:46.910
We're not gonna go faster
than the speed of light,

00:00:46.910 --> 00:00:48.530
but we could easily imagine

00:00:48.530 --> 00:00:49.930
that the human lifespan gets extended

00:00:49.930 --> 00:00:52.450
to thousands of years,
and once you do that,

00:00:52.450 --> 00:00:54.500
then the stars are much
closer, effectively, right?

00:00:54.500 --> 00:00:56.570
And then what's a
hundred-year trip, right?

00:00:56.570 --> 00:00:58.767
So I think that that's
gonna be the future,

00:00:58.767 --> 00:01:01.665
the far future, not my
lifetime, once again,

00:01:01.665 --> 00:01:03.700
but baby steps and then.

00:01:03.700 --> 00:01:05.740
- Unless your lifetime gets extended.

00:01:05.740 --> 00:01:07.730
- Well, it's in a race
against time, right?

00:01:07.730 --> 00:01:09.970
A friend of mine you actually thinks about

00:01:09.970 --> 00:01:13.657
these things said, "You know,
you and I are gonna die,

00:01:13.657 --> 00:01:15.807
"but I don't know about
our grandchildren."

00:01:17.230 --> 00:01:18.120
I don't know.

00:01:18.120 --> 00:01:19.270
Predicting the future is hard,

00:01:19.270 --> 00:01:20.909
but that's at least a plausible scenario.

00:01:20.909 --> 00:01:25.120
And so, yeah, no, I think
that, as we discussed earlier,

00:01:25.120 --> 00:01:27.860
there are threats to the earth, known

00:01:27.860 --> 00:01:29.484
and unknown, right?

00:01:29.484 --> 00:01:34.484
Having spread humanity
and biology elsewhere

00:01:35.880 --> 00:01:38.380
is a really important long-term goal.

